    {
      "id": "2X966Ls0u8TpJGVK0bHdE",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 485.2973606937321,
      "y": 6791.824646873117,
      "width": 1035.359375,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#4dabf7",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2G",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 116647164,
      "version": 201,
      "versionNonce": 1240608781,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1774973555781,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A star schema is a mature modeling approach originating from relational data warehouses, where data \nis classified into facts (measurable, quantitative data) and dimensions (descriptive attributes). \nIt's a way of organizing data so that the metrics (like sales amount or quantity) sit in the center table, \nand the descriptions (like customer name, date, or product details) sit in smaller tables around it—\nlooking exactly like a star. it is implemented using relational tables with enforced primary key-foreign \nkey constraints to optimize read performance and simplify aggregations for downstream BI tools.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A star schema is a mature modeling approach originating from relational data warehouses, where data \nis classified into facts (measurable, quantitative data) and dimensions (descriptive attributes). \nIt's a way of organizing data so that the metrics (like sales amount or quantity) sit in the center table, \nand the descriptions (like customer name, date, or product details) sit in smaller tables around it—\nlooking exactly like a star. it is implemented using relational tables with enforced primary key-foreign \nkey constraints to optimize read performance and simplify aggregations for downstream BI tools.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "wspGU0wjbVckoMpJXaWW2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 477.99358653002514,
      "y": 7648.884038130492,
      "width": 999.0392456054688,
      "height": 325,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2I",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1943641232,
      "version": 419,
      "versionNonce": 281365485,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1774972128358,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Down at the infrastructure level, Database stores these tables relationally in \neither Row-store format  or Columnstore format When queried, \nthe query optimizer recognizes the primary-to-foreign key relationships. \nIt creates an execution plan optimized for star joins, often using hash or merge joins\n\n\nStar schemas denormalize the data - which means adding redundant columns to some dimension tables \nto make querying and working with the data faster and easier. \n\ntrade-off b/w - some redundancy for increased speed \nby avoiding computationally expensive join operations.\n\nIn this model, the fact table is normalized but the dimensions tables are not. ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Down at the infrastructure level, Database stores these tables relationally in \neither Row-store format  or Columnstore format When queried, \nthe query optimizer recognizes the primary-to-foreign key relationships. \nIt creates an execution plan optimized for star joins, often using hash or merge joins\n\n\nStar schemas denormalize the data - which means adding redundant columns to some dimension tables \nto make querying and working with the data faster and easier. \n\ntrade-off b/w - some redundancy for increased speed \nby avoiding computationally expensive join operations.\n\nIn this model, the fact table is normalized but the dimensions tables are not. ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
